{"name":"Spoonful of Sugar","hex":"#e7e9e3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spoonful","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The amount that a spoon will hold, either level or heaped."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spoonful"},{"term":"sugar","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A food consisting of small, sweet crystals, principally of sucrose, obtained from sugar cane or sugar beet and used as sweetener and preservative.","Any specific variety of sugar."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To add sugar to; to sweeten with sugar.","To make (something unpleasant) seem less so."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sugar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spoonful of Sugar (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Spoonful of Sugar is a 2022 American horror thriller film that was directed by Mercedes Bryce Morgan, based on a script written by Leah Saint Marie. It stars Morgan Saylor, Kat Foster, Danilo Crovetti, Myko Olivier and Keith Powell. The film centers on a college student who takes on a job caring for a sickly child, only for things to go horribly wrong when she offers him some of her own medication."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0f/Spoonful_of_Sugar_%28film%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spoonful_of_Sugar_(film)","wikidata":"Q117286417"},{"title":"A Spoonful of Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"\"A Spoonful of Sugar\" is a song from Walt Disney's 1964 film and 2004 musical version of Mary Poppins, composed by Robert B. Sherman and Richard M. Sherman. The song has characteristics of the fast-paced one-step, a popular dance in the 1910s."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/18/Spoonful_of_Sugar_45_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Spoonful_of_Sugar","wikidata":"Q4659764"},{"title":"Spoonful","blocks":[{"text":"\"Spoonful\" is a blues song written by Willie Dixon and first recorded in 1960 by Howlin' Wolf. Called \"a stark and haunting work\", it is one of Dixon's best known and most interpreted songs. Etta James and Harvey Fuqua had a pop and R&B record chart hit with their duet cover of \"Spoonful\" in 1961 and it was popularized in the late 1960s by the British rock group Cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Spoonful_by_howlin_wolf_us_vinyl_side-a.png/330px-Spoonful_by_howlin_wolf_us_vinyl_side-a.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spoonful","wikidata":"Q2096323"},{"title":"Sugar","blocks":[{"text":"Sugar is a class of sweet-tasting, soluble carbohydrates, many of which are used in food. Simple sugars, also called monosaccharides, include glucose, fructose and galactose. Compound sugars, also called disaccharides or double sugars, are molecules made of two bonded monosaccharides; common examples are sucrose, lactose and maltose. White sugar is almost pure sucrose. During digestion, compound sugars are hydrolysed into simple sugars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg/330px-Sucre_blanc_cassonade_complet_rapadura.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sugar","wikidata":"Q11002"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Spoonful_by_Cream_Australian_single_side_A.png/500px-Spoonful_by_Cream_Australian_single_side_A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Spoonful_by_Cream_Australian_single_side_A.png/500px-Spoonful_by_Cream_Australian_single_side_A.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F